From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: pinephone: ramoops

A RAM region for pstore, so that the log of a panic (or of a hang the
lockup detectors turn into one) shows up in /sys/fs/pstore on the next
boot. Without a serial cable that is the only way to see why the phone
hung, e.g. in suspend.

Only a SoC watchdog reset keeps the RAM: the kernel's restart goes
through PSCI to Crust, which restarts the PMIC, RAM supply included
(tested: a word written there is noise after sysrq-b, kept after the
watchdog fired). So leave kernel.panic at 0 and let /dev/watchdog,
opened and no longer fed, do the reset.

1 MiB at 1.5 GiB, away from where U-Boot loads the kernel, device tree
and initramfs (0x40080000 to 0x50000000), from U-Boot itself (relocated
below 2 GiB with its heap and stack: a region just under 0x80000000 was
lost on every restart) and from the power-of-two offsets the SPL probes
for the RAM size. ECC so that a few bits lost in the reset do not cost
the record.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
@@ -19,6 +19,22 @@
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 	};
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <1>;
+		ranges;
+
+		ramoops@60000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x60000000 0x100000>;
+			record-size = <0x40000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x10000>;
+			ecc-size = <16>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
 	backlight: backlight {
 		compatible = "pwm-backlight";
 		pwms = <&r_pwm 0 50000 PWM_POLARITY_INVERTED>;
